  CALIBRATION RANGE OF THE KERNEL.  SPARC (147 galaxies, 3140 points, hunt_lib.load_sparc):
     canonical: fitted over y = 2.23e-03 to 78.4, i.e. sqrt(y) <= 8.86
           alt: fitted over y = 1.85e-03 to 65.0, i.e. sqrt(y) <= 8.06
    the planets sit at sqrt(y) = 835 (Saturn) to 20562 (Mercury).
    Route A's exponent sqrt(y) is therefore extrapolated by a factor 94x (Saturn) to 2322x (Mercury) beyond the largest value any fitting datum has.

